Above. See <Before-Prae>.

Abraham.; Abraham.

@SE 206. That Abraham does not know us. Explanation.

@AE 768[13]. "Abraham" = the Lord as to the Divine Celestial of the Church... (therefore) "the seed of Abraham" = Divine truth celestial.

@--[14]. That "the seed of Abraham" does not mean the Jews, is evident from... (John 8:33-44). Here, "Abraham" means the Lord, and "the seed of Abraham", Divine truth from the Lord, which is the Word... "I know that ye are Abraham's seed" = that the Lord knew that the truth of the Church, which is the Word, was among them... (and also because) Judah = the Lord as to the Word.

